                    <chunk name="param_input" index="5">
                      <items count="9">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">How many processes the Radiance chain spreads its sensors over.
The annual matrix multiplies (dctimestep + rmtxop) are ~60% of the chain and scale with sensor count — at 4500 sensors they are most of the run — and neither program has a threading flag, so running several over slices of the sensors is the only way to use more than one core on them.
Auto (default) picks one process per core, never splitting below 500 sensors a block. Off runs the single-process chain exactly as it was before this existed.
This never changes the answer: every sensor is traced by identical commands against identical octrees and sky matrices; only which file it was listed in differs.
Only applies when Radiance Reflections is on.</item>
