                    <chunk name="param_input" index="6">
                      <items count="7">
                        <item name="Access" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">1</item>
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Optional hours of the year (1-8760, e.g. from the HOY component) the study is about. EnergyPlus then simulates only the days spanning them, plus 3 lead-in days, instead of the whole year — its cost is close to linear in simulated hours, so a heat-wave week runs many times faster.
The MRT result is still 8760 hours: outside the period the surrounding surfaces are assumed to sit at air temperature, exactly as with EnergyPlus Surfaces off, so read results only for the hours given here. A selection that wraps the new year runs (nearly) the whole year. Empty (default) = full year.
Only applies when EnergyPlus Surfaces is on. The Radiance chain works on annual sky matrices and is not shortened by this.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">e6ed99ae-5b7f-4e21-a34f-d0adaf1bd68e</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Run Period</item>
                        <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">HOY</item>
                        <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                        <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                      </items>
                      <chunks count="1">
                        <chunk name="Attributes">
                          <items count="2">
                            <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                              <X>906</X>
                              <Y>1666</Y>
