                            </item>
                          </items>
                        </chunk>
                      </chunks>
                    </chunk>
                    <chunk name="param_input" index="7">
                      <items count="6">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">true (default): the Radiance chain moves its annual matrices as binary files and the sun term is finished as a sparse product on the host — several times quicker on large sensor grids, a quarter of the disk, and free of the three-digit rounding ASCII sky matrices carry (up to 0.5 % of the beam in an hour).
false: the ASCII chain Eddy3D shipped before this input existed, kept as the control and the way back. For Two-Phase DDS the two agree to float rounding apart from that rounding. Two-Phase (preview) reads its beam straight from the sampled ray-traced coefficients, which the ASCII chain does not reproduce from run to run (about 0.7 % of the annual total, and more in single hours); the binary chain does.
Only applies when Radiance Reflections is on.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">c657056b-ad3c-4691-81aa-e99d67e71d85</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Fast Matrices</item>
                        <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Fast</item>
                        <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                        <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                      </items>
                      <chunks count="2">
                        <chunk name="Attributes">
