                    </chunk>
                    <chunk name="param_input" index="8">
                      <items count="9">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Which Two-Phase (daylight-coefficient) method the Radiance chain runs.
Two-Phase DDS (default): the sun is traced separately, one source per fine sky bin (Bourgeois, Reinhart and Ward 2008), so shadows have close to the sun's own edges.
Two-Phase (preview): the sun is read off the 145-patch sky, spread over the four patches nearest it, so shadow edges are blurred by several degrees and hourly beam and dMRT at sun altitudes below about 8 degrees are approximate. It skips the sun trace: about twice as quick on a grid of a few hundred sensors or more (five times on a handful). Reflected and diffuse light are the same; the annual total stayed within 2-3 % of Two-Phase DDS on the test cube and can differ more in a street canyon. For choosing a layout, not for a result.
Scenes with tree crowns always run Two-Phase DDS.
Only applies when Radiance Reflections is on.</item>
