                    <chunk name="param_input" index="9">
                      <items count="9">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">How finely the sky is divided for the traced sun of Two-Phase DDS (the Reinhart subdivision).
MF:4 (default): 2,305 suns, bins about 3 degrees across.
MF:6: 5,185 suns, about 2 degrees: the traced sun lands closer to the real one (the hourly error of the beam against an exact solar position fell by about a fifth in the check this setting was added with), for about twice the sun-coefficient trace and twice the disk of the transfer matrix.
Ignored by Two-Phase (preview) and by scenes with tree crowns.
Only applies when Radiance Reflections is on.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">30096fa7-e877-413d-9ff1-1a3f8968da11</item>
