                    <chunk name="param_input" index="0">
                      <items count="10">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Which climate file to use. Click the widget and choose Weather file (catalog)… to pick from the catalog with a map and a spec sheet; the value stored is the file's own name (e.g. DEU_BE_Berlin-Tempelhof.AP.103840_TMYx.2009-2023). A station name, WMO id, country or dataset year still works as a search — the best match nearest the site wins — and a direct EPW or ZIP URL is downloaded as-is. Choose Open-Meteo (ERA5) — or type Open-Meteo 2019 — to build a file for the SITE (wire Latitude/Longitude, or set the Earth Anchor Point) from ERA5 reanalysis: one actual year, last year unless one is given, on the 0.25° cell. Weather data by Open-Meteo.com (CC BY 4.0).</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">bb2489ac-ba82-4dd0-ab48-d172c13aed40</item>
